Patch 7930: the UI_SCALE box reads the HUD vertex positions with a streaming load (UI_BOX_NT, on by default).

vp_record_cb read every HUD vertex's position back from the vertex upload heap, which is write-combined memory: each
plain load goes all the way to RAM (2 Players 3v3: 16 % of the drawing thread). One 16-byte streaming load (MOVNTDQA,
made for reading write-combined memory) per vertex instead. Same values, same box, same picture. UI_BOX_NT=0: plain
loads as before.
Measured on replays: 2 Players 3v3 35.71 -> 31.73 ms, 2v2 16.31 -> 14.58 ms, pictures bit-exact. HUD sizes 1.00 /
0.75 / 0.50, Hide HUD and the 3v3 Character Select layout looked the same in real runs.

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
index 87a376e..92e8db6 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
@@ -5401,6 +5401,22 @@ static void fpk_fill(u32 fp_addr, const u8* code, float* out)
     if (m->nk) memcpy(out, m->k, (size_t)m->nk * 16);
 }
 
+/* UI_BOX_NT (=0 off): the UI_SCALE box below reads each vertex's position back from the vertex
+ * upload heap, which is write-combined memory: every plain load there goes all the way to RAM (2 Players 3v3: 16 % of
+ * the drawing thread). One 16-byte streaming load (MOVNTDQA, made for reading write-combined memory) per vertex instead.
+ * Same values, same box. */
+#include <immintrin.h>
+static int ui_box_nt_on(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) { const char* e = getenv("UI_BOX_NT"); on = (e && *e == '0') ? 0 : 1; }
+    return on;
+}
+__attribute__((target("sse4.1"))) static inline void ui_nt_load16(const void* p, float out[4])
+{
+    const __m128i v = _mm_stream_load_si128((__m128i*)p);
+    _mm_storeu_si128((__m128i*)out, v);
+}
 static void vp_record_cb(u32 slot, int vs_idx, const D3D12DrawRecord* dr)
 {
     const rsx_state* st = s_d3d.current_rsx_state;
